  "rationale": "O12 (N2, docs/CASESTUDY.md): a challenge adds proofWindow W to the finalize deadline of every other unfinalized batch (Rollup.sol:485-495), and pausing deletes the open challenge but keeps those extensions (Rollup.sol:575-583), so the undo pair (challengeState, setPause(true)) is REFUTED (L_undo_cancel). The extensions are the protocol's design: every challenge buys the challenged batch's peers one more proof window. The contract bounds them as intended: on M2's window view of the extracted Rollup, every batch's finalize deadline is at most its commit time plus F plus W for each challenge that succeeded so far (the ghost counter, a sum of W over the successful challengeState steps of the trace). The two further conjuncts are the facts the bound's induction needs and are true of the code: a challenge is open only after one succeeded, and the open challenge started in the past. A batch committed while a challenge is open gets the remaining window, at most W (Rollup.sol:360-364).",
